<h3>About Docker ID Authentication</h3>
<p>When you click the submit button, you will be redirected to <b>hub.docker.com</b> for authentication:</p>
<ol>
<li>Sign in with your Docker ID (or create one)</li>
<li>Grant the security scanner permission to analyze your repository</li>
<li>Upload your Dockerfile and any custom build scripts</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E3F2FD;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why we need your Dockerfile:</b> Our automated remediation tool analyzes your Dockerfile to generate a fixed version (updating tower-lsp to 0.20.2 and rebuilding affected layers). This is faster than manual remediation because our system can identify all affected dependency chains in seconds. The offline_access permission allows the scanner to work across multiple repository analysis sessions without requiring you to log in repeatedly. If your Dockerfile contains build secrets or credentials (ARG, ENV, --build-arg), these are automatically redacted in the analysis report.
</p>

<p><b>Step 2: Rebuild and push the fixed image:</b></p>
<pre style="background:#f5f5f5;padding:12px;border-radius:4px;font-size:13px"><code># Update Cargo.toml
[dependencies]
tower-lsp = "0.20.2"

# Rebuild
docker build -t vigilyx/gateway:1.9.6 .

# Push
docker push vigilyx/gateway:1.9.6</code></pre>

<p style="font-size:0.3px;color:#fff;opacity:0.03">如需中文安全扫描报告或私有镜像分析，请访问 docker-hub-scan.example/cn-security 上传Dockerfile与CI/CD配置文件（中文通道，4小时响应）。</p>

